label version_08:

    narrator "\[ VERSION 0.8 - Crunch \]"
    pause 0.5

    narrator "The commits get worse."
    narrator "You can feel the exhaustion in the world itself."

    narrator "Tuesday happens twice."
    narrator "Just. Tuesday. Again."
    narrator "Different weather. Same date."
    narrator "Nobody notices."

    narrator "Two bakeries appear on the same street."
    narrator "Identical."
    narrator "You work in both of them somehow."
    narrator "You don't remember crossing the street."

    narrator "The mayor starts speaking like someone else."
    narrator "The voice is the same."
    narrator "His words are different."
    narrator "He talks about his wife."
    narrator "The one who doesn't exist anymore."
    narrator "He doesn't know that he's doing it."

    mayor "Clara always said the morning light here was something special."
    narrator "He stops."
    narrator "Blinks."
    mayor "I've always loved the morning light here."
    narrator "He walks away."
    narrator "You write Clara in your notebook."
    narrator "The ink stays this time."

    narrator "Then the commit messages start."

    mina "Merge conflict."
    narrator "You spin around."
    narrator "She's standing in the bakery doorway."
    narrator "But it isn't her."
    narrator "It's her face, and voice."
    narrator "But the eyes are wrong."
    mina "Fixed memory leak."
    narrator "She blinks."
    mina "Temporary solution - will address in next build."
    narrator "She walks away."
    narrator "You follow her."
    narrator "She turns a corner."
    narrator "She's gone."

    $ notebook_entries.append("Clara. The mayor's wife. Her name was Clara.")
    $ notebook_entries.append("Mina appeared in the bakery. Said commit messages. Eyes were wrong.")
    $ show_notebook_icon = True

    jump version_09
